    - **Launch timer today** `Utilities.GetAircraftCooldown` (aircraft count x `aircraftLaunchCooldown`, plus count x `aircraftLaunchPayloadCooldown` with a payload). In `config.txt` `aircraftLaunchCooldown` is 0 and `aircraftLaunchPayloadCooldown` is 180 seconds per aircraft, so aircraft without a payload (fighters, scouts) launch with no timer at all. That is the gap. Applied by `CampaignManager.ApplyCooldownToAirLauncher` (airfield: `MapLocation.aircraftCooldown`; ship: `MobileMapObject.aircraftCooldown[shipIndex]`) and, for the enemy, in `CampaignAI` (around line 1422). First step may be only raising these two config values.
    - **Landing timer today** `CampaignManager` (around line 3349) adds `aircraftLandCooldown` (240 seconds) per aircraft to the airfield's `MapLocation.aircraftCooldown` when aircraft land. Only airfields get it, a landing on a carrier adds nothing. That is why a carrier can relaunch straight away. Aircraft destroyed use `aircraftDestroyedCooldown` (600).
